I really love the phone booth.  Most excelent!  Love the superhero too, but
it's too powerfull for the game.

Here's more ideas:

Madam's House of Pleasure
=========================
A house full (your discression) of succubi that give you a variety of favors
but you pay in advance.  Can cause level gains for new comers, sickness,
confusion (*love?), and other strange things.  Ruled by a madame that sells
you stuff on the side (like potions of ???), whip, strange garments of
clothes, you can imagine.  +2 whip of pleasure?

Radio
=====
Plays music (notes), gives you broadcasts of god, attracts monsters, multiple
chanels, news ads for shopkeepers on the same or different levels, general
dance mayhem (rock stations are equal to the ring of conflict), peacefull
channels (elevator music makes monsters fall asleep).  Blessed radios
allow you to tune into your local god, cursed radios don't turn off and make
you deaf.

Beach
=====
This level would be covered with water, and would allow you to try out
those new magic items you've been dying to try out: ring of surfing, 
surfboard (blessed surfs like a pro, cursed tips over and breaks the
string, tangling you up and drowning), shorts of swimming, potion of
beer (makes you more charismatic or appealing), sunblock of all colors
(protects from the *sun* *dragon/demon fire* whatever).  Lots of sand
everywhere and maybe a lot of sexy @s (guys and gals in small pieces of
clothing -- maybe even the bronze bikini!)  Guys selling you stuff on
the shore, what have you.

Theatre
-------
Almost always a dark room, you can watch the movie (learn new things
or whatever, cures the blues (sickness), makes you sick (horror movies),
makes you jumpy (action).  Find gross things on the floor, or maybe a
wallet or some loose change.  Lots of monsters watching, don't get in
their way or they might breath on you to get you to sit down.  Might
even tell you hints (like fortune cookies) on how to make magic items
(if Excalibur was playing, could drop some hints about dipping the sword
in the water; if Indina Jones was playing, might give you hints on using
your whip [Archiologists], Wizards would teach Wizards how to use a gun,
you get the picture).

Shrink
======
Cures you of your alignment problems (if you're chaotic or lawful).  Charges
you a bill.

Bard
====
This new class from AD&D would give you a musical instrument to charm
the hell from beneath your feet.  Starts with +0 chainmail, a long sword,
a couple of spells, a magical instrument, a scroll or two, and a nice
feather hat.  High charisma and definitely a pet or two.  Maybe even a 
music book or a song book. "You find a blessed book of ballads."  "You find
a songbook of Stairway to Heaven."  Playing the notes backwards will summon
a demon or send you straight to hell.  Special abilities include charm
monster, please crowd, whatever musicians do.  Angels could sing you songs
when you pray, fortune cookies could give you hints "play g c e a backwards
to remove sickness from your cat or dog" g c e a is "my dog has fleas".

Pizza Boy
=========
This class starts with a blessed bag of holding and 24 pizzas to eat or
to deliver.  A bunch of scrolls (some blank, some with orders for the
various monsters, shopkeepers, demons, and maybe even the wizard!) that
tell you what level they live on.  Some $ to make change, monsters that
mug you, monsters that don't pay, some that don't like your pizza, some
that get angry when you don't deliver them on time.  Maybe even some
mystic pizza!  Monsters will let you walk without harm (most of the time),
succubusses will want to share food.  Walkman optional.  Must wear the
silly Domino's hat to get safe passage through the dungeon.

Terminator
==========
Just like the Arnold movie of the future.  No succubuses please!  High
strength, low dexterity, lots of built in armor, low wisdom, average
intelligence.  Doesn't need food (120 year battery).  Likes lots of guns.
Default intrinsics include fast, poison resistant, rust resistant (stainless
steel?), sleep resistant, see invisible (infra-red).  Couple of high
and low calibur weapons.  Magic resistant.  No memorized spells.  Maybe
a leather jacket +1.  Maybe his mission is to kill the wizard instead
of getting the amulet.  Maybe his mission is to kill all @s he finds.  Nurses
hate this guy.  Definitely chaotic (nasty firmware!).


The terminator could also be a nasty monster!  Ignores you if you're 
polymorphed into something non-human.  Always attacks humans, wizards, 
and other human look alikes (succubusses too).  Keeps saying "Sara Connor?"
Just doesn't get it right.

Copy machine!
=============
Can Xerox scrolls!  Most of them will come out blank.  Paper jams (scroll
is lost!).  Cursed scrolls could come out.  Likes scrolls of blank paper.
Many to be found near by.  Needs $ to make it work.  Copier could be out of
paper too.  No toner.  Scrolls all black (too much toner!)

Traffic Cop!
============
Hands out scrolls (usually cursed).  Don't kill him, or the keystone cops
will be out to get you.  "Do you know why I stopped you?"  Must listen to
cop; just like the mimic, you can't run away.  If a cop is nearby, "You hear
a siren" or "you hear a motorcycle nearby" or "stop, or I'll shoot!".
Could be a terminator in disguise!  Definitely notices unpaid items from
storekeepers "Hack's 10 most wanted." "Don't I know you from level 4?"
"Let me run your ID through."  "No ID?  You're coming with me..."

Robo-cop
========
A combination terminator/cop.  "Dead or alive, you're coming with me."
Lot's of armor, lots of determination, lot's of bullets.  If you're a nice
citizen, it leaves you alone.  Likes lawful and neutrals.  Hates chaotics.
Puts you in jail and reads you your rights.

Judge Dread
Judge Dread
============
Just like the comics, judge and juror on the spot.  If your god is angry,
he's definitely on your case.  If your god is happy, will find something
to convict you of right on the spot.  Not a ver nice guy.

Con-Man (aka the traveling salesman)
====================================
Tries to sell you cheap copies of the amulet of Amdor.  Maybe even a couple
of Rolex watches.  Watch out for your credit card.  Likes to steal $.  Maybe
killing him will give you lots of $ and cheap stuff.  Definitely an overcoat
(to hide the goodies) and a leather hat.  Nice snakeskin or lizard boots.
Cops are always nearby to find this guy.  Will arrest you too for talking
to him.

Newsperson
==========
Bugs you for intervies.  Traveling crew flashes you with cameras and
bright lights (makes you blind all the time!).  "Talking to the reporters
makes you sick." "You see a bright flash of light."  "You hit the reporter."
"You hit the reporter."  "You break his nose."

Tourist
=======
As a monster, he likes to use the camera often on you.  "You see a bright
flash of light."  Just like the newsperson.

Santa-Claus
===========
Not recommending any religious persuasion.  Carries a bag of holding and
lots of goodies to get.  If you are nice (good standing with your god), he
will give you a present.  If you are naughty, zippo dude!  Mugging this guy
is definitely a good thing for the chaotic.  Maybe some raindeer too "You hear
the sounds of many hoves from above."  "You hear a ho-ho-ho nearby."
"You hear a laughter like a bowl full of jelly."  Whatever.  "You hear
a jingle nearby."

7-11
====
Never closed, high prices, lots of normal goodies.  Cola, soda, food
rations (never spoiled!).  Some tins, a can opener, and a big gulp in all
flavors (potions!).  Scrolls (magazines).  A place to spend that gold
when you're out of luck.  Always has things in stock.  Cops hang out in
front having donuts.  "You buy a potion of slime mold juice."

Hand Grenade
============
Like the search for the Holy Grail, you can have one too!  The Holy Grenade
comes encrusted with lots of jewels (which you get when it blows up).  Wipes
out lots of monsters.  Lots of fun.

Jedi
====
This new class has a light saber, some defensive spells (at higher levels).
Looks for the amulet because it "contains the force."  Wizard is his
father.  Obi or Yoda pops fortune cookie type messages in his head
Yoda says "The wizard may be found on this level."  High dex, high wisdom,
average intelligence.  Mechanical arm optional.


Solo
====
Cyberpunk fans everwhere!  This is the class you want to be!  Lots of
built-in intrinsics (mitsubishi eyes -- see invisible, Sony ears -- hear
monsters in a 100 meter radius, boosted reflexes -- super human dexterity,
hand razors -- better hand-to-hand damage, chipped intrinsics).  Low 
charisma (everone hates a solo).  Good weapons and that super-cool look!
Leather jacket and sunglasses a must!  Immune to all kinds of stuff.  Another
guy who has problems using spells.  Starts off cursed in some way.  That's
why he became a solo in the first place.  No dog required.  Definitely 
chaotic.  Artifical arms give boosted strength.  Weapons like "Your
monofilament whip hits the shopkeeper!  You destroyed the shopkeeper!"

Well, some crazy ideas.  What do you think?

